{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (+0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"HARD ANODIZING"}],"comment":"The ⌀16 H7 hole (D12) carries a tight ISO fit on a part that is hard anodized, but the drawing does not account for the coating thickness in the tolerance band. The anodize buildup will shrink the bore and can cause the mating shaft to no longer fit; the designer must either adjust the pre-coating size/tolerance or add a note to mask or re-machine the hole after anodizing."
    ,
    "recommended_correction":"Adjust the pre-anodize hole size to allow for coating thickness, or specify masking/re-machining of the ⌀16 H7 bore after hard anodizing."}]}
